# dbt

## Naming (from engineering_standards.md §1)

- Staging: `stg_<source>__<entity>`
- Base: `base_<domain>__<entity>`
- Core: `dim_<entity>`, `fct_<entity>`
- Intermediate: `int_<domain>__<purpose>`
- Marts: `mart_<domain>__<purpose>`
- Columns: snake_case; booleans `is_`/`has_`; timestamps `_at`; dates `_date`

## Where rules live (do not re-derive here)

- Layer contract: [`docs/layering.md`](../../docs/layering.md)
- Testing, SQL structure, CI gate: [`docs/engineering_standards.md`](../../docs/engineering_standards.md)
- Stock-specific: [`docs/project_context.md`](../../docs/project_context.md)

## Mandatory guardrails

- `1_staging`: one `stg_*` model per raw source table; no cross-source joins.
- Staging SQL under `models/1_staging/<source>/`, never at `1_staging/` root.
- `4_intermediate` must not `ref('mart_*')`.
- Every model starts with import CTEs; named CTE chains only.
- Every new model needs at least one meaningful test.

## Tooling

- Sync registry → dbt vars: `python scripts/sync_dbt_vars.py`
- Layer contract: `python scripts/check_layer_contract.py`
